---
title: "Row Grouping - Editing Groups"
enterprise: true
---

The Grid supports editing of grouped data when using the
[Client-Side Row Model](./row-models/#client-side). When users edit values in grouped columns,
the grid can automatically refresh the grouping hierarchy to reflect the changes.

## Refreshing Groups After Editing

When grouped columns are editable, enable `refreshAfterGroupEdit=true` to update the row data and
regroup after each group field edit.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Refresh After Group Edit" name="refresh-after-group-edit" exampleHeight=600 /%}

In the example above, changing the `region` causes the grid to re-evaluate the grouping and move
the row to the correct group instantly. Double click on a `region` cell to edit it.

By default, without `refreshAfterGroupEdit` enabled, the row data updates but the grouping does not
get updated until the next full refresh.

When enabling `refreshAfterGroupEdit`, it is recommended to also set `getRowId` so that the grid can
track rows by stable IDs while rebuilding the grouping hierarchy.

See also [Read Only Edit](./value-setters/#read-only-edit) for configuring immutable grouped data or
connecting the grid with a store.

## Editing Group Row Cells

Add `groupRowEditable` to any column that should accept edits on group nodes.
This value can be a boolean (true or false) or a callback that will only be called for nodes where `rowNode.group === true`, while leaf rows continue to rely on
`editable`.

`groupRowValueSetter` is a callback similar to `valueSetter`, but specifically for group rows.
It is called whenever a group row cell is edited, whether via the UI, `rowNode.setDataValue` and can be used to cascade the edit to child rows.

When users edit cells via the UI, the grid runs the full value pipeline: `valueParser`, `valueSetter`,

When a column defines both `groupRowEditable` and `editable`, AG Grid only evaluates the property
that matches the current node type, enabling separate rules for group rows and leaves.

## Custom Aggregation Value Setters

Aggregated columns can stay editable by providing a `valueSetter` that pushes committed values
down to descendants and lets the normal aggregation rebuild the totals. Pair this with
`groupAggFiltering=true` so group rows track the same filtered subset the grid displays. The example
below shows the full pattern, including a `valueParser`, recursion guard, and filter-aware
distribution.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Editable Group Totals" name="group-row-editable-totals" exampleHeight=620 /%}

Key points:

- Use `groupRowValueSetter` to redistribute committed values to descendants. The callback receives the
	group row node and column, runs whether the edit originated from the UI, `setDataValue`, or a
	read-only edit request, and can return `false` to cancel the commit after performing validation.
- `rowNode.setDataValue` on children to update a child value, this triggers normal aggregation to refresh the parent totals and recurses further down if is a group invoking its own
	`groupRowValueSetter`.
- `rowNode.childrenAfterSort` lists only descendants in the node to update. This can contain groups or leafs.
	adjust exactly the rows the user can see, and clearing the filters leaves untouched nodes as-is.
- Parent aggregates refresh automatically because the children’s `data` changes trigger the column
	`aggFunc`, so typing £600 at “Europe” rebalances the filtered countries to reach that total.

